  "reply": "`parseDuration` in `src/duration.ts` now accepts the format you described, and `bun test` passes (26 tests, 0 failures). I changed only that file.\n\n- **Accepted input:** one or more components in strictly descending `h`, `m`, `s`, `ms` order, with optional whitespace between components and at both ends. The result is the total in milliseconds.\n- **Rejected input:** it throws `RangeError` for empty input, duplicate or out-of-order units, signs, fractions, and any leftover junk. It also throws when a single value or the running total exceeds `Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER`.\n- **Overflow handling:** I used `BigInt` for the arithmetic so large values can't lose precision before the check.\n- **API:** the `parseDuration` export and its signature are unchanged, and the library stays dependency-free as `CLAUDE.md` requires.\n\nI didn't add tests of my own, so the overflow limits are covered only if the existing 26 tests include them.",
